---
/**
 * The starting-price disclaimer. Must appear wherever prices appear.
 *
 * Publishing prices is this site's differentiator, but a published number
 * creates an obligation: the customer must not walk away thinking one price
 * covers every door and every fault. A single door and a double door are
 * different jobs, and so are a slipped cable and a snapped one.
 *
 * `variant="inline"` is the short asterisk line for tables and cards.
 * `variant="block"` is the fuller explanation for service and price pages.
 */
interface Props {
  variant?: 'inline' | 'block';
}
const { variant = 'inline' } = Astro.props;
---
{variant === 'inline' ? (
  <p class="price-note-inline">
    <span aria-hidden="true">*</span> Starting prices for a standard single door.
    Your final price depends on the door, the model and what we find. You get a
    written quote before any work starts.
  </p>
) : (
  <aside class="price-note-block" aria-label="How our pricing works">
    <h3><span aria-hidden="true">*</span> How to read these prices</h3>
    <p>
      Every number on this site is a <strong>starting price</strong> for a
      standard single garage door in normal condition. It is a real number, not
      a teaser, and it is where a straightforward job begins.
    </p>
    <p>What moves your price above the starting point:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Door size.</strong> A double door is a bigger job than a single door, with more parts and more weight.</li>
      <li><strong>Door type and model.</strong> Materials, brands and discontinued models change what the parts cost and whether they are even available.</li>
      <li><strong>Condition.</strong> A failure rarely happens alone. Cables, drums, rollers and brackets that failed alongside are quoted before we replace anything.</li>
      <li><strong>Access and timing.</strong> Difficult access, and emergency or after-hours calls, carry their own cost, stated up front.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="price-note-promise">
      What does not change: you get a written quote before any work begins, and
      that quote is the price you pay. We do not name a low number to get in the
      door and then raise it once the door is apart.
    </p>
  </aside>
)}

<style>
  .price-note-inline {
    font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--c-muted);
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
  }
  .price-note-inline span { color: var(--c-accent-dark); font-weight: 800; }

  .price-note-block {
    background: var(--c-bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--c-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0;
  }
  .price-note-block h3 { font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .price-note-block h3 span { color: var(--c-accent-dark); }
  .price-note-block p { font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .price-note-block ul { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .price-note-block li { font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .price-note-promise {
    margin-bottom: 0; padding-top: 0.7rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    font-weight: 600; color: var(--c-ink);
  }
</style>
